@title Telemetry pipeline architecture
@subtitle Skerry Wind Power · Owner: Asset Data team · Region eu-north-1 · Reviewed 2026-10-02

## Overview
Turbine readings flow from each of our 6 offshore wind farms into one central stream, where they are processed once. The processed data is then split into a fast store for dashboards and a cheap archive for audits.

## Pipeline diagram
diagram telemetry dir=LR title="Telemetry pipeline"
telemetry: tc "Turbine Controllers" ext "On site, each farm"
telemetry: eg "Edge Gateway" svc "On site, each farm"
telemetry: ts "Telemetry Stream" queue
telemetry: sp "Stream Processor" svc focus
telemetry: tsdb "Timeseries Store" db
telemetry: raw "Raw Archive" store
telemetry: alert "Alerting Service" svc
telemetry: dash "Operations Dashboard" svc
telemetry: group cloud "Cloud account" ts, sp, tsdb, raw, alert, dash
telemetry: tc -> eg : OPC UA, 1 Hz
telemetry: eg -> ts : MQTT over TLS, batched every 5 s
telemetry: ts -> sp : consumer
telemetry: sp -> tsdb : 10 s aggregates
telemetry: sp -> raw : Parquet every 15 minutes
telemetry: sp -> alert : threshold breach
telemetry: tsdb -> dash : queries
telemetry: legend

## Capacity and retention
- **Telemetry Stream**: 24 shards, 18000 messages per second at peak
- **Timeseries Store**: 7 days in memory, then 3 years on magnetic storage
- **Raw Archive**: 10 years, moved to cold storage after 90 days

## If the uplink fails
The Edge Gateway buffers up to 6 hours of readings on disk. When the link returns, it replays them in order.

!! After 6 hours, the oldest readings are dropped. Readers must not miss this limit.
